@startuml
title Data model
hide empty members
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

class Frame <<envelope>> {
  from : string
  to : string
  timestamp : int64 (sender clock, ms)
  ciphertext : bytes (base64)
  signature : bytes (base64)
}

class Payload <<encrypted>> {
  from : string
  text : string
}

class CryptoModule <<module>> {
  keygen() : KeyPair
  encrypt(key, msg) : bytes
  decrypt(key, msg) : bytes
  hash(data) : bytes
  sign(privateKey, hash) : bytes
  verify(publicKey, hash, sig) : bool
}

class "keys" as Keys <<table>> {
  name : TEXT <<PK>>
  public_key : TEXT
}

class "messages" as Messages <<table>> {
  sender : TEXT
  recipient : TEXT
  timestamp : INTEGER
  frame : TEXT
}

Frame ..> Payload : ciphertext =\nencrypt(recipient key, JSON(payload))
CryptoModule ..> Frame : builds, signs,\nverifies, decrypts
Messages ..> Frame : stores verbatim in "frame";\nother columns are unverified copies\nof from, to, timestamp (log readability only)
Keys ..> CryptoModule : public keys fetched via\nGET /keys/{name}, used for\nencrypt and verify

note bottom of Frame
  from is right-padded with padding to a fixed width (32 bytes)
  before hashing, so every field has a fixed position:

  signature = sign(H( pad(from, 32) || timestamp || ciphertext ))

  "to" is deliberately unsigned
end note

note bottom of Keys
  Registration enforces a username charset/length
  that makes the padding above unambiguous:
  1-32 bytes, no padding byte, 8-bit character encoding.
end note

note bottom of Messages
  Server never queries this table.
  Hidden rowid gives arrival order.
end note
@enduml
